    "created_at": "2024-03-05T18:39:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-05T18:39:19Z",
    "body": "There may be an error when the scale is powered off or turned back on which would require you to call `port.readable.getReader()` again. For example, the scale may generate a \"break\" signal at power-on. Does your code handle errors returned by the reader and request a new reader on the new `ReadableStream` returned by `port.readable` in that case?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
